id=a52sxq_camera_stability
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: hal3_mass camera stability (Single Take crash, vendor key spam, PPP draft insert)
author=kusti420
description=Smali fixes for UN1CA's r9qxxx SamsungCamera 16.0.00.74 ("hal3_mass" flavor, installed by unica/patches/camera because TARGET_CAMERA_SUPPORT_MASS_APP_FLAVOR=true). Camera sweep 2026-10-23 (9.3.72). The work is in apply.sh, run from target/a52sxq/post_mods.sh: device patches run before unica/patches, and the camera only exists (and is decoded) once unica/patches/camera ran. 1. Single Take crashed the app on every entry (3/3, FATAL "There is no main session" in RecordingSessionManagerImpl.getMainSession <- prepareRecording <- PrepareMediaRecorderRequest, ~90 ms after tapping SINGLE TAKE in MORE, no record key involved). Cause: the S26U floating feature GALLERY_CONFIG_AI_EXPANSION carries "singletake.video.previous_record", which this app maps to SUPPORT_SINGLE_TAKE_VIDEO_PREVIOUS_RECORDING; PrepareVideoMakerRequest then takes the Single Take service record surface and creates no RecordingSession, but mode 37 (SINGLE_TAKE_VIDEO, the only Single Take mode in the A52s camera-feature.xml) is SingleTakeVideoFeature, whose isMediaRecorderRequired() is true, so PREPARE_MEDIA_RECORDER runs against an empty session map. Stock A52s and S21 FE have no such flag. The app's reader of that flag (x1.e.m0 in this build) returns false, so Single Take records through its normal MediaRecorder session as on the S21 FE; the floating feature itself is left alone (Gallery reads it). Safety net: RecordingSessionManagerImpl.prepareRecording() checks for a main session first and, without one, logs and throws the app's own media recorder prepare exception (I2.a code 2), which PrepareMediaRecorderRequest already catches (onRecordingFailed, request discarded) instead of crashing the process. 2. SemCaptureResult.a() (the vendor CaptureResult getter) catches the IllegalArgumentException CameraMetadataNative throws for a key with no vendor tag on this HAL, logs it with VendorTagDescriptor's lookup error, and is asked again on the next frame: samsung.android.lens.info.generalLensType and originalFocalLengthIn35mmFilm (S21 FE / One UI 7+ tags) are read on every preview/video frame, ~28 exceptions per second at 30 fps. A key whose lookup failed with "Could not find tag for key" is remembered by name (process-wide set) and returns null at once afterwards, which is what the caller got anyway; keys that exist are read exactly as before. 3. One UI 9 MediaProvider rejects a post-processing draft insert (sef_file_type 2928) unless is_drm is 1 ("PPP needs to set the is_drm to prevent uploading to the cloud", MediaDao.checkValuesForPPP requires is_drm == 1, not 0), so Portrait/processed captures fell back to the recovery path. Prepared but OFF by default (K4_CAMERA_PPP_DRM=1 at build time enables it): PostSavingModuleSecMpInsert's draft insert would put is_drm=1, as the S26U camera's own draft insert does, but it is not verified yet that the finished photo ends with is_drm=0; until a device test shows that, drafts keep falling back (the photo is saved either way).
